  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    # size of the grid\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows else 0\n    \n    # centre line (integer division)\n    centre_row = rows // 2\n    centre_col = cols // 2\n    \n    # find the outermost positions of the upper\u2011left and lower\u2011right clusters\n    max_row_top = -1          # greatest row index that is above the centre\n    min_row_bottom = rows     # smallest row index that is below the centre\n    max_col_left = -1         # greatest column index left of the centre\n    min_col_right = cols      # smallest column index right of the centre\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v == 0:\n                continue\n            # vertical side\n            if r < centre_row:\n                if r > max_row_top:\n                    max_row_top = r\n            elif r > centre_row:\n                if r < min_row_bottom:\n                    min_row_bottom = r\n            # horizontal side\n            if c < centre_col:\n                if c > max_col_left:\n                    max_col_left = c\n            elif c > centre_col:\n                if c < min_col_right:\n                    min_col_right = c\n    \n    # shift distance = floor(half the gap between the two clusters)\n    vertical_shift = 0\n    if max_row_top >= 0 and min_row_bottom < rows:\n        vertical_shift = (min_row_bottom - max_row_top) // 2\n    \n    horizontal_shift = 0\n    if max_col_left >= 0 and min_col_right < cols:\n        horizontal_shift = (min_col_right - max_col_left) // 2\n    \n    # build the output grid\n    out = [[0] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v == 0:\n                continue\n            \n            # new row\n            if r < centre_row:\n                nr = r + vertical_shift\n            elif r > centre_row:\n                nr = r - vertical_shift\n            else:\n                nr = r\n            \n            # new column\n            if c < centre_col:\n                nc = c + horizontal_shift\n            elif c > centre_col:\n                nc = c - horizontal_shift\n            else:\n                nc = c\n            \n            out[nr][nc] = v\n    \n    return out",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    # size of the grid\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows else 0\n    \n    # centre line (integer division)\n    centre_row = rows // 2\n    centre_col = cols // 2\n    \n    # find the outermost positions of the upper\u2011left and lower\u2011right clusters\n    max_row_top = -1          # greatest row index that is above the centre\n    min_row_bottom = rows     # smallest row index that is below the centre\n    max_col_left = -1         # greatest column index left of the centre\n    min_col_right = cols      # smallest column index right of the centre\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v == 0:\n                continue\n            # vertical side\n            if r < centre_row:\n                if r > max_row_top:\n                    max_row_top = r\n            elif r > centre_row:\n                if r < min_row_bottom:\n                    min_row_bottom = r\n            # horizontal side\n            if c < centre_col:\n                if c > max_col_left:\n                    max_col_left = c\n            elif c > centre_col:\n                if c < min_col_right:\n                    min_col_right = c\n    \n    # shift distance = floor(half the gap between the two clusters)\n    vertical_shift = 0\n    if max_row_top >= 0 and min_row_bottom < rows:\n        vertical_shift = (min_row_bottom - max_row_top) // 2\n    \n    horizontal_shift = 0\n    if max_col_left >= 0 and min_col_right < cols:\n        horizontal_shift = (min_col_right - max_col_left) // 2\n    \n    # build the output grid\n    out = [[0] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v == 0:\n                continue\n            \n            # new row\n            if r < centre_row:\n                nr = r + vertical_shift\n            elif r > centre_row:\n                nr = r - vertical_shift\n            else:\n                nr = r\n            \n            # new column\n            if c < centre_col:\n                nc = c + horizontal_shift\n            elif c > centre_col:\n                nc = c - horizontal_shift\n            else:\n                nc = c\n            \n            out[nr][nc] = v\n    \n    return out",
